  "l_space_justification": {
    "citation": "P. Ozsvath and Z. Szabo, On the Heegaard Floer homology of branched double-covers, Advances in Mathematics 194 (2005), 1-33, Theorem 1.1 and Corollary 1.2.",
    "url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0309170",
    "doi": "10.1016/j.aim.2004.05.008",
    "statement": "The spectral sequence from reduced Khovanov homology of the mirror over F_2 to HFhat of the double branched cover gives det(K) <= rank HFhat(Sigma_2(K); F_2) <= rank Kh_reduced(K; F_2). Mirror symmetry preserves total rank. Equality of the tabulated reduced mod-2 rank with the determinant therefore establishes the L-space hypothesis over F_2."
  },
